X: 1
T: Belle qui tiens ma vie
C: Thoinot Arbeau, Orchesographie (Langres, 1589)
O: France, 16th century
N: The pavane from Arbeau's dancing manual, printed there with the drum
N: pattern beside it. Melody and chords come from the four-voice setting
N: (Nicolas Graner's transcription of the 1589 print) -- the chords are the
N: harmony Arbeau's lower three voices actually sing. Transposed up a fifth.
L: 1/8
Q: 1/2=56
M: 4/4
K: F
